  "solution": {
    "explanation": "At each house choose between skipping it (keep the best so far) and robbing it (add its value to the best from two houses back). Keep those two best-so-far values in variables and roll them forward. One pass, so O(n) time and O(1) space. A brute-force recursion without memoisation is exponential.",
    "code": "class Solution:\n    def rob(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        prev, cur = 0, 0\n        for x in nums:\n            prev, cur = cur, max(cur, prev + x)\n        return cur\n"
  }
